### Test file for Touch Grass API Authentication Endpoints
### Use with REST Client extension in VS Code or similar HTTP client

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### ===========================
### Health Check
### ===========================

### Check server health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Get API information
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Privacy policy parents accept
GET {{baseUrl}}/privacy

### ===========================
### Authentication Endpoints
### ===========================

### 1. Signup - Parent Account (consent to the privacy policy is required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "parent@test.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "consent": true
}

### 2. Parent: create a kid's login (replace KID_ID; use a parent token)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/kids/KID_ID/login
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "sam",
  "pin": "0420"
}

### 3. Login - Parent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "parent@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 4. Login - Kid (familyCode from the parent signup)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/kid-login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "familyCode": "A3F2B1",
  "username": "sam",
  "pin": "0420"
}

### 5. Delete account (parent): removes the parent and all their kids' data
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Get Current User (Protected - requires token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### ===========================
### Kid Profile Endpoints
### ===========================

### Parent: add a kid (consent required; interests, username and pin optional)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/kids
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ann",
  "age": 6,
  "interests": ["swimming"],
  "consent": true,
  "username": "ann",
  "pin": "1234"
}

### Parent: list kids
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/kids
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Parent: get / update / delete a kid (replace KID_ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/kids/KID_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Kid: get own profile (use a kid token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/kids/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Kid: update own avatar and interests
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/kids/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "avatarColor": "from-green-400 to-teal-500",
  "interests": ["soccer", "climbing"]
}

### ===========================
### Game Endpoints
### ===========================

### Kid: my adventure (use a kid token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/game/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Kid: submit a challenge
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/game/me/challenges/backyard-bug-hunt
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": "Found a beetle, a worm and a snail!"
}

### Parent: approvals waiting (use a parent token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/game/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Parent: a kid's adventure (replace KID_ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/game/kids/KID_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Parent: approve or reject (replace COMPLETION_ID; decision is approve or reject)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/game/completions/COMPLETION_ID/review
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "approve"
}

### ===========================
### Error Test Cases
### ===========================

### Kid signup - refused (403): parents create kid logins
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "kid2@test.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "kid"
}

### Signup - no consent (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "noconsent@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Kid login - wrong PIN (401; 5 in a row locks it for 15 minutes)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/kid-login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "familyCode": "A3F2B1",
  "username": "sam",
  "pin": "9999"
}

### Malformed kid id (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/kids/not-an-id
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Signup - Missing password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "error@test.com"
}

### Signup - Password too short
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "consent": true,
  "email": "short@test.com",
  "password": "12345"
}

### Signup - Invalid email format
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "consent": true,
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Signup - Invalid role
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "consent": true,
  "email": "invalid-role@test.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "admin"
}

### Signup - Duplicate email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "consent": true,
  "email": "parent@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Login - Wrong password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "parent@test.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Login - Non-existent user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Get Current User - No token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### Get Current User - Invalid token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token_here

### ===========================
### Instructions
### ===========================

# 1. Start MongoDB (if running locally):
#    mongod
#
# 2. Start the server:
#    npm run dev
#
# 3. Test the endpoints in order:
#    - First, signup a new user
#    - Copy the token from the response
#    - Replace {{token}} at the top of this file
#    - Test the protected /me endpoint
#
# 4. Use REST Client extension in VS Code to run these requests
#    Or use Postman, Insomnia, or curl
